---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How Mass Spectrometry Components Are Manufactured: From Drawing to Finished Part"
  description="See how custom mass spectrometry components move from drawing review and precision machining to inspection, cleaning and finished production."
>
  <article>
    <header class="relative overflow-hidden bg-navy-950 text-white">
      <div class="grid-bg absolute inset-0 opacity-20"></div>
      <div class="absolute -right-28 -top-48 h-130 w-130 rounded-full border border-blue-300/20"></div>
      <div class="container-wide relative py-18 md:py-24">
        <p class="mb-6 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[.22em] text-blue-300">Technical guide</p>
        <h1 class="max-w-5xl text-4xl font-semibold leading-[1.07] tracking-[-.045em] sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl">
          How Mass Spectrometry Components Are Manufactured: From Drawing to Finished Part
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300">
          A practical overview of drawing review, process planning, precision machining, inspection, cleaning, and finished production.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="bg-white py-14 md:py-20">
      <div class="mx-auto w-[calc(100%-2rem)] max-w-3xl">
        <div class="space-y-6 text-[1.02rem] leading-8 text-slate-700">
          <p>Mass spectrometry components often require more than conventional CNC machining. Dimensional accuracy, surface condition, cleanliness, vacuum compatibility and instrument integration may all affect the performance of the finished system.</p>
          <p>At Maisi Precision, our technical team has hands-on experience in mass spectrometry component manufacturing, assembly, customization and applications. This helps us approach each component not simply as a machined part, but as part of a precision analytical instrument.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-14 space-y-14 md:mt-18 md:space-y-18">
          <section>
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-[-.035em] text-navy-950">1. Drawing Review</h2>
            <div class="mt-6 space-y-5 leading-8 text-slate-700">
              <p>Manufacturing starts with the customer drawing.</p>
              <p>Dimensions, tolerances, interfaces, materials and surface requirements are reviewed together with the component's intended application. Understanding how a part functions within the instrument helps identify critical manufacturing and inspection requirements before production begins.</p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-[-.035em] text-navy-950">2. Material &amp; Process Planning</h2>
            <div class="mt-6 space-y-5 leading-8 text-slate-700">
              <p>Depending on customer requirements, Maisi works with materials including 304/316L stainless steel, aluminum alloys, oxygen-free copper, titanium alloys, ceramics and PEEK.</p>
              <p>The machining process is planned according to part geometry, precision requirements, surface requirements and production quantity.</p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-[-.035em] text-navy-950">3. Precision Machining</h2>
            <div class="mt-6 space-y-5 leading-8 text-slate-700">
              <p>Mass spectrometry systems contain mechanical components with widely different geometries and functions. Each part therefore requires an appropriate machining strategy based on its drawing and application.</p>
              <p>Maisi supports prototypes, small batches and repeat production of custom components for mass spectrometry and scientific instrumentation.</p>
            </div>

          </section>

          <section>
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-[-.035em] text-navy-950">4. Inspection &amp; Cleaning</h2>
            <div class="mt-6 space-y-5 leading-8 text-slate-700">
              <p>Critical dimensions and features are inspected against customer drawings, with attention to interfaces and characteristics that may affect instrument assembly.</p>
              <p>For components used in vacuum and high-vacuum environments, Maisi also provides appropriate cleaning processes for high-vacuum and UHV-related applications.</p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-[-.035em] text-navy-950">5. Finished Components</h2>
            <div class="mt-6 space-y-5 leading-8 text-slate-700">
              <p>After machining, inspection and required cleaning or finishing, components are prepared for delivery according to customer requirements.</p>
              <p>Our manufacturing experience covers mechanical parts throughout mass spectrometry systems, including components associated with ion sources, ion optics, mass analyzers, vacuum systems and other custom assemblies.</p>
            </div>

          </section>

          <p class="leading-8 text-slate-700">From drawing review to finished production, each step contributes to the quality and consistency of a mass spectrometry component. By combining precision manufacturing with practical mass spectrometry experience, Maisi Precision aims to help instrument manufacturers turn component designs into reliable, production-ready parts.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <section class="bg-navy-800 text-white">
    <div class="container-wide flex flex-col gap-7 py-12 md:flex-row md:items-center md:justify-between">
      <div>
        <p class="mb-3 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[.2em] text-blue-200">Discuss your project</p>
        <h2 class="max-w-3xl text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-.035em] md:text-4xl">Have a Component Drawing to Evaluate?</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-blue-100">If you are developing a mass spectrometry system or looking for an additional manufacturing supplier, we would be glad to review your drawings and manufacturing requirements.</p>
        <a href="mailto:engineering@msprec.com" class="focus-ring mt-3 inline-block text-sm font-medium text-blue-100 underline decoration-blue-300 underline-offset-4 hover:text-white">engineering@msprec.com</a>
      </div>
      <a href="/contact#quote" class="focus-ring inline-flex shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-white px-7 py-4 font-semibold text-navy-950 transition hover:bg-blue-50">
        Send us your drawing for manufacturing review and quotation. <span class="ml-3" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
